From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: pinch zooms the page; Meta+pinch magnifies the desk

Pinch works as on a Mac. A two-finger pinch magnifies the page under
the pointer, and Meta+pinch or Meta+scroll magnifies the whole desk.

- `CrossProcessFrameConnector::GetPinchZoomTarget` gives a <webview>'s
  page, the main frame of an inner WebContents, its own pinch, as a
  browser tab has. Upstream hands it to the outermost page, the desk.
  A page that takes the pinch's ctrl+wheel keeps it, and an `<app>`
  still forwards it to its native client (patch 0184).
- `RenderWidgetHostViewAura::GestureEventAck` no longer forwards an
  unconsumed touchpad pinch to the desk's page scale, so a plain pinch
  over the shell does nothing.
- `RenderWidgetHostInputEventRouter` sends a pinch begun with Meta held
  straight to the root view's page scale, without hit testing or the
  wheel step. Meta+scroll becomes a pinch on the root, doubling the
  magnification every 300 pixels; its momentum is dropped.
- libinput (`EventFactoryEvdev`) and the host
  (`WaylandEventSource`) put the keyboard's modifiers on pinch
  events, so the router can see Meta.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
